[[:db/retract 17592186133266 :answer-field/choices 17592186133267] [:db/retract 17592186133266 :answer-field/choices 17592186133268] [:db/retract 17592186133266 :answer-field/choices 17592186133270] [:db/retract 17592186133266 :answer-field/choices 17592186133271] {:db/id 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6056a54f-50c5-51bf-9c90-30d0151550be" "question-b199a74a-63a2-5637-aa94-6d70ba2bd918" "question-d87af21c-48b4-5612-ae7a-18902b89c926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133516 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n![](images/17/1714eb4797f7b318f5e957db7ab0f322fffb2eb2c9bf03f68e3acc08ec399849.svg)\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x \\geq 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/4f/4f0d336b322f68550c50d65380e26ffb33bdd55beab0c7d429e7b4055f973b57.svg)\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/9e/9e1b63a37177781672b70c3a6c01b1b752164b976b6e9982e07d510d468353aa.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aa0570cf-0a8d-5b19-8cfc-d1d338d11235" "question-fb64e84b-4036-56ed-b5be-3b99c498406f" "question-ae38bc39-2bd5-58c3-af2b-ad65de482c6d" "question-dbdaccde-7824-5d29-93f1-f05b495a99f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133517 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x) = e^{-|2x|}, \\quad x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/40/40ebced9e322ef969e40733356aacdb3971e14276bc6ad54691aeea21b14c488.svg)\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x \\leq 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x > 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/92/9293ff0dab0e6c12fd143ec5f8a9d72edfce74fcddae2397f19d0e82a8b767cc.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" "question-d8d29abd-ea88-5ad4-8655-fbf6ab67a44c" "question-298016d0-4ea6-54d8-a832-231f3f8e4443" "question-9853f7b8-7c5d-5c25-8113-542fa8b8a6a4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133518 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n![](images/9d/9d755ff833ca8a9134d8f2548b6e7e26221a4814cda8a28093a345a2d321920e.svg)\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0 \\leq x \\leq 12,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/fd/fd6306e35f5c55b4de635fe7d8967e7783f11c96cee2ea8adfdd17348f97a095.svg)\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{72}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{144}{t}^{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{144}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/b1/b168cb9b6e4619e7b25cddea9ee671e665d057923b9562ff50d99ce874ea8b90.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" "question-83a3d348-6693-5dcc-af5c-61cd638a0bb7" "question-3ffe741c-4355-5cb4-a113-2fae2e76fdee" "question-502fa5ed-8192-5239-85ce-b51fd4a6a69d" "question-de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133519 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n![](images/97/9792a5033ccd5f6f8198e3465899c752ddd4ae0986b324c13575c1a92e1ff3c7.svg)\n\nfind $P(2\\leq X \\leq 6).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 6) & =P(2<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-25}{75}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{75}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-6056a54f-50c5-51bf-9c90-30d0151550be" :question/id #uuid "6056a54f-50c5-51bf-9c90-30d0151550be" :question/math-academy-id "q-89652" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{6}{{t}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{6}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a835c292-a833-5026-9266-1d083a85fb56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a835c292-a833-5026-9266-1d083a85fb56" :answer-field/id #uuid "a835c292-a833-5026-9266-1d083a85fb56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f215aa0-6421-5dd2-9e39-875332acba0c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a0c5aada-ee2d-584d-bd82-102f09606a74" "answer-b97304b0-2f60-5182-8a38-e54a262d9d43" "answer-5f215aa0-6421-5dd2-9e39-875332acba0c" "answer-1608a6a2-ef7d-5264-a5b5-e47796062000" "answer-6fdf2e24-d0fd-503f-a916-289e0fb74567"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0c5aada-ee2d-584d-bd82-102f09606a74" :answer/id #uuid "a0c5aada-ee2d-584d-bd82-102f09606a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b97304b0-2f60-5182-8a38-e54a262d9d43" :answer/id #uuid "b97304b0-2f60-5182-8a38-e54a262d9d43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f215aa0-6421-5dd2-9e39-875332acba0c" :answer/id #uuid "5f215aa0-6421-5dd2-9e39-875332acba0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1608a6a2-ef7d-5264-a5b5-e47796062000" :answer/id #uuid "1608a6a2-ef7d-5264-a5b5-e47796062000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{42}{{x}^{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fdf2e24-d0fd-503f-a916-289e0fb74567" :answer/id #uuid "6fdf2e24-d0fd-503f-a916-289e0fb74567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134538 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{t}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{x}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133266 :answer-field/correct "answer-9212ec56-6681-5b9b-8850-605544afb5ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9212ec56-6681-5b9b-8850-605544afb5ba" "answer-86dc2cb8-34c2-59e1-b615-ac22c665e6f0" "answer-1d135339-50d4-589a-bbdd-9dfafdad32ca" "answer-7dac7e0d-2683-504c-998e-6a8f2452bc74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9212ec56-6681-5b9b-8850-605544afb5ba" :answer/id #uuid "9212ec56-6681-5b9b-8850-605544afb5ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86dc2cb8-34c2-59e1-b615-ac22c665e6f0" :answer/id #uuid "86dc2cb8-34c2-59e1-b615-ac22c665e6f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d135339-50d4-589a-bbdd-9dfafdad32ca" :answer/id #uuid "1d135339-50d4-589a-bbdd-9dfafdad32ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dac7e0d-2683-504c-998e-6a8f2452bc74" :answer/id #uuid "7dac7e0d-2683-504c-998e-6a8f2452bc74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b199a74a-63a2-5637-aa94-6d70ba2bd918" :question/id #uuid "b199a74a-63a2-5637-aa94-6d70ba2bd918" :question/math-academy-id "q-89641" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8{x}^{4}},\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2},$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}\\frac{3}{8{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{8{t}^{3}}|}_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d15e4d33-3d39-5536-93e8-49947424a563"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d15e4d33-3d39-5536-93e8-49947424a563" :answer-field/id #uuid "d15e4d33-3d39-5536-93e8-49947424a563" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-998775fa-da47-5947-a129-bd6df19698f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-712de365-0023-5929-82ba-68a165ee7cd6" "answer-998775fa-da47-5947-a129-bd6df19698f4" "answer-447da342-1533-5f2c-8730-3f4fcfb6eb1b" "answer-8bb2a535-9d88-5742-8c31-810ff3deadc7" "answer-cbb15cdc-5bd3-5d38-9b32-45651985451c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-712de365-0023-5929-82ba-68a165ee7cd6" :answer/id #uuid "712de365-0023-5929-82ba-68a165ee7cd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{32{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-998775fa-da47-5947-a129-bd6df19698f4" :answer/id #uuid "998775fa-da47-5947-a129-bd6df19698f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-447da342-1533-5f2c-8730-3f4fcfb6eb1b" :answer/id #uuid "447da342-1533-5f2c-8730-3f4fcfb6eb1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bb2a535-9d88-5742-8c31-810ff3deadc7" :answer/id #uuid "8bb2a535-9d88-5742-8c31-810ff3deadc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbb15cdc-5bd3-5d38-9b32-45651985451c" :answer/id #uuid "cbb15cdc-5bd3-5d38-9b32-45651985451c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d87af21c-48b4-5612-ae7a-18902b89c926" :question/id #uuid "d87af21c-48b4-5612-ae7a-18902b89c926" :question/math-academy-id "q-89546" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e86a899-b91b-5d71-978f-830f6bac2bb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e86a899-b91b-5d71-978f-830f6bac2bb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e86a899-b91b-5d71-978f-830f6bac2bb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9121cbd0-f9a1-5785-bcd2-b0cf0a5368c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce921dda-8563-59de-b3fe-a15f6ce57053" "answer-4b6bc818-cf5d-5fbf-8f54-469f90018d9d" "answer-9121cbd0-f9a1-5785-bcd2-b0cf0a5368c0" "answer-ae3913fb-6c1f-5066-a107-fc615c4d98c4" "answer-baa7e096-af04-58c0-9b33-2d21728b4311"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce921dda-8563-59de-b3fe-a15f6ce57053" :answer/id #uuid "ce921dda-8563-59de-b3fe-a15f6ce57053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b6bc818-cf5d-5fbf-8f54-469f90018d9d" :answer/id #uuid "4b6bc818-cf5d-5fbf-8f54-469f90018d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9121cbd0-f9a1-5785-bcd2-b0cf0a5368c0" :answer/id #uuid "9121cbd0-f9a1-5785-bcd2-b0cf0a5368c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae3913fb-6c1f-5066-a107-fc615c4d98c4" :answer/id #uuid "ae3913fb-6c1f-5066-a107-fc615c4d98c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{2}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baa7e096-af04-58c0-9b33-2d21728b4311" :answer/id #uuid "baa7e096-af04-58c0-9b33-2d21728b4311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134158 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}6{e}^{-6x},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}6{e}^{-6t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-6t}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6x}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ 1-{e}^{-6x}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131062 :answer-field/correct "answer-38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde" :answer-field/choices ["answer-38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde" :answer/id #uuid "38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e^{-6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134159 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\n$F(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{t}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131063 :answer-field/correct "answer-b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer/id #uuid "b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa0570cf-0a8d-5b19-8cfc-d1d338d11235" :question/id #uuid "aa0570cf-0a8d-5b19-8cfc-d1d338d11235" :question/math-academy-id "q-89631" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2x})},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2t})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{t}}{\\pi }|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a631477-d8b0-5499-9e18-4bec118a663c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a631477-d8b0-5499-9e18-4bec118a663c" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a631477-d8b0-5499-9e18-4bec118a663c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" "answer-9506108c-e704-538c-b725-308070b7259a" "answer-c702e577-7142-5b26-9822-367c7f969cb4" "answer-4f0f787d-1687-5d7b-90fc-bcc440b2102f" "answer-e9553f1f-e879-592c-9f68-96e639709428"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" :answer/id #uuid "6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9506108c-e704-538c-b725-308070b7259a" :answer/id #uuid "9506108c-e704-538c-b725-308070b7259a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c702e577-7142-5b26-9822-367c7f969cb4" :answer/id #uuid "c702e577-7142-5b26-9822-367c7f969cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f0f787d-1687-5d7b-90fc-bcc440b2102f" :answer/id #uuid "4f0f787d-1687-5d7b-90fc-bcc440b2102f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}-1}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9553f1f-e879-592c-9f68-96e639709428" :answer/id #uuid "e9553f1f-e879-592c-9f68-96e639709428" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb64e84b-4036-56ed-b5be-3b99c498406f" :question/id #uuid "fb64e84b-4036-56ed-b5be-3b99c498406f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210762" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{e}^{-|4x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\le 0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals. \n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn particular, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2},\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fea0be10-7e7a-5e8c-b225-cbbbd6502e43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fea0be10-7e7a-5e8c-b225-cbbbd6502e43" :answer-field/id #uuid "fea0be10-7e7a-5e8c-b225-cbbbd6502e43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cc767f0c-f65c-5d40-bf26-8221c3e5652f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cc767f0c-f65c-5d40-bf26-8221c3e5652f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc767f0c-f65c-5d40-bf26-8221c3e5652f" :answer/id #uuid "cc767f0c-f65c-5d40-bf26-8221c3e5652f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{e^{-4x}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae38bc39-2bd5-58c3-af2b-ad65de482c6d" :question/id #uuid "ae38bc39-2bd5-58c3-af2b-ad65de482c6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89635" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{3}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f84d8dbb-e4a3-55af-a310-662430392d90"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f84d8dbb-e4a3-55af-a310-662430392d90" :answer-field/id #uuid "f84d8dbb-e4a3-55af-a310-662430392d90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4b0ae796-f204-5f28-ae72-68cb7f93938e" "answer-170a0edf-da7f-5652-903d-c47b4ac8c342" "answer-cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" "answer-3a8d1627-2737-5252-95ce-1a7d32a52868" "answer-095360e1-dd96-5383-931f-a201eff47a39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b0ae796-f204-5f28-ae72-68cb7f93938e" :answer/id #uuid "4b0ae796-f204-5f28-ae72-68cb7f93938e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1+\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-170a0edf-da7f-5652-903d-c47b4ac8c342" :answer/id #uuid "170a0edf-da7f-5652-903d-c47b4ac8c342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1+\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" :answer/id #uuid "cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a8d1627-2737-5252-95ce-1a7d32a52868" :answer/id #uuid "3a8d1627-2737-5252-95ce-1a7d32a52868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-095360e1-dd96-5383-931f-a201eff47a39" :answer/id #uuid "095360e1-dd96-5383-931f-a201eff47a39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dbdaccde-7824-5d29-93f1-f05b495a99f8" :question/id #uuid "dbdaccde-7824-5d29-93f1-f05b495a99f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126213" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{4{e}^{2x}}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{3}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05df3ca1-c837-5b2a-a2ca-c614521b137f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05df3ca1-c837-5b2a-a2ca-c614521b137f" :answer-field/id #uuid "05df3ca1-c837-5b2a-a2ca-c614521b137f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e57de798-83cd-5d70-b368-ec17bdf4fd1b" "answer-0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" "answer-794e5508-c708-5544-83e6-85e9c8ebed21" "answer-0b1e4645-ce48-5f06-a7d7-34323e0d0b93" "answer-83be2e46-de7d-50e1-912e-11e66409165a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e57de798-83cd-5d70-b368-ec17bdf4fd1b" :answer/id #uuid "e57de798-83cd-5d70-b368-ec17bdf4fd1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1+\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" :answer/id #uuid "0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-794e5508-c708-5544-83e6-85e9c8ebed21" :answer/id #uuid "794e5508-c708-5544-83e6-85e9c8ebed21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b1e4645-ce48-5f06-a7d7-34323e0d0b93" :answer/id #uuid "0b1e4645-ce48-5f06-a7d7-34323e0d0b93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83be2e46-de7d-50e1-912e-11e66409165a" :answer/id #uuid "83be2e46-de7d-50e1-912e-11e66409165a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134150 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{21}x,\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{21}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{21}{t}^{2}|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131036 :answer-field/correct "answer-65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f" :answer/id #uuid "65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}-4}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" :question/id #uuid "dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-210788" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f" :answer-field/id #uuid "fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer/id #uuid "9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d8d29abd-ea88-5ad4-8655-fbf6ab67a44c" :question/id #uuid "d8d29abd-ea88-5ad4-8655-fbf6ab67a44c" :question/math-academy-id "q-210786" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{60}{x}^{3},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{1}{60}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{240}|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{240}-\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{4}}{240}-\\frac{1}{15}, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b8a4a48c-0c9e-5eff-a6c5-6bb8647bf693"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b8a4a48c-0c9e-5eff-a6c5-6bb8647bf693" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a4a48c-0c9e-5eff-a6c5-6bb8647bf693" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-92696a8b-4d36-591b-8359-09b0462c87c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92696a8b-4d36-591b-8359-09b0462c87c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92696a8b-4d36-591b-8359-09b0462c87c2" :answer/id #uuid "92696a8b-4d36-591b-8359-09b0462c87c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}-16}{240}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-298016d0-4ea6-54d8-a832-231f3f8e4443" :question/id #uuid "298016d0-4ea6-54d8-a832-231f3f8e4443" :question/math-academy-id "q-210784" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{x}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 2,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}(1-\\frac{t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37f12d01-f36a-528a-8df0-5d27379297ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37f12d01-f36a-528a-8df0-5d27379297ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "37f12d01-f36a-528a-8df0-5d27379297ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49" :answer/id #uuid "5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9853f7b8-7c5d-5c25-8113-542fa8b8a6a4" :question/id #uuid "9853f7b8-7c5d-5c25-8113-542fa8b8a6a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-89664" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{15}(6-x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{15}(6-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{15}t(t-12)|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}x(x-12)-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+12x-20}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{-{x}^{2}+12x-20}{15}, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43d0599e-de67-5781-8910-15575fd37739"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43d0599e-de67-5781-8910-15575fd37739" :answer-field/id #uuid "43d0599e-de67-5781-8910-15575fd37739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3713bbf7-8cf6-556f-9963-5d4f811dfef6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-907813c6-ec0c-5b8a-a9ca-a322238090df" "answer-3713bbf7-8cf6-556f-9963-5d4f811dfef6" "answer-e53e4edf-d1ef-53f7-aa8f-37ab74e89205" "answer-7579f568-8475-5f5b-8c86-9498d6ae9355" "answer-df7344a3-6751-5056-8424-2ea934d23b3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-907813c6-ec0c-5b8a-a9ca-a322238090df" :answer/id #uuid "907813c6-ec0c-5b8a-a9ca-a322238090df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+12x-8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3713bbf7-8cf6-556f-9963-5d4f811dfef6" :answer/id #uuid "3713bbf7-8cf6-556f-9963-5d4f811dfef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-{x}^{2}+12x-20}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e53e4edf-d1ef-53f7-aa8f-37ab74e89205" :answer/id #uuid "e53e4edf-d1ef-53f7-aa8f-37ab74e89205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-10x-8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7579f568-8475-5f5b-8c86-9498d6ae9355" :answer/id #uuid "7579f568-8475-5f5b-8c86-9498d6ae9355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df7344a3-6751-5056-8424-2ea934d23b3d" :answer/id #uuid "df7344a3-6751-5056-8424-2ea934d23b3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-12x-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" :question/id #uuid "3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126177" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{225}{(x+15)^{2}}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{225}{(5+15)^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f3a27a8-4efa-5646-b1d9-f25fb627f5fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f3a27a8-4efa-5646-b1d9-f25fb627f5fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f3a27a8-4efa-5646-b1d9-f25fb627f5fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6d30549b-41ec-5746-94b1-bdf0fddb2247" "answer-04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" "answer-35abf0ef-ee66-53cd-a97d-5575de5686bc" "answer-22307ec9-ce6b-54ac-8d2e-3cf6990bb045" "answer-0f9b63be-e003-513c-960b-dc0a6866add4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d30549b-41ec-5746-94b1-bdf0fddb2247" :answer/id #uuid "6d30549b-41ec-5746-94b1-bdf0fddb2247" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" :answer/id #uuid "04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35abf0ef-ee66-53cd-a97d-5575de5686bc" :answer/id #uuid "35abf0ef-ee66-53cd-a97d-5575de5686bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{225}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22307ec9-ce6b-54ac-8d2e-3cf6990bb045" :answer/id #uuid "22307ec9-ce6b-54ac-8d2e-3cf6990bb045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f9b63be-e003-513c-960b-dc0a6866add4" :answer/id #uuid "0f9b63be-e003-513c-960b-dc0a6866add4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83a3d348-6693-5dcc-af5c-61cd638a0bb7" :question/id #uuid "83a3d348-6693-5dcc-af5c-61cd638a0bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-89746" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-6x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(5\\le X\\le 8).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5\\le X\\le 8) & =P(5<X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8)-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(8)-F(5) \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-48}-(1-{e}^{-30}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-30}-{e}^{-48}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac8d7e22-8e94-5eb5-a89b-c464e93eefa6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac8d7e22-8e94-5eb5-a89b-c464e93eefa6" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac8d7e22-8e94-5eb5-a89b-c464e93eefa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-813bdb77-ccc7-5860-9046-506a4f6e91a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6127124c-024d-5286-8963-795ce40b1454" "answer-588e72ed-c4d3-5982-8daf-db7b4cfb2955" "answer-813bdb77-ccc7-5860-9046-506a4f6e91a5" "answer-d018b541-4be1-5c04-b19b-380ff23fb6ce" "answer-c2583976-feec-54f6-a03e-5fbf264986d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6127124c-024d-5286-8963-795ce40b1454" :answer/id #uuid "6127124c-024d-5286-8963-795ce40b1454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-({e}^{-30}-{e}^{-48})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-588e72ed-c4d3-5982-8daf-db7b4cfb2955" :answer/id #uuid "588e72ed-c4d3-5982-8daf-db7b4cfb2955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-30}+{e}^{-48}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-813bdb77-ccc7-5860-9046-506a4f6e91a5" :answer/id #uuid "813bdb77-ccc7-5860-9046-506a4f6e91a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-30}-{e}^{-48}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d018b541-4be1-5c04-b19b-380ff23fb6ce" :answer/id #uuid "d018b541-4be1-5c04-b19b-380ff23fb6ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-30}-{e}^{48}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2583976-feec-54f6-a03e-5fbf264986d3" :answer/id #uuid "c2583976-feec-54f6-a03e-5fbf264986d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{30}-{e}^{-48}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ffe741c-4355-5cb4-a113-2fae2e76fdee" :question/id #uuid "3ffe741c-4355-5cb4-a113-2fae2e76fdee" :question/math-academy-id "q-89700" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-x}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(2<X\\le 4).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 4) & =P(X\\le 4)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(2) \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}-(1-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8abf257c-5f7a-58cf-ac37-0d4ffd9399e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8abf257c-5f7a-58cf-ac37-0d4ffd9399e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "8abf257c-5f7a-58cf-ac37-0d4ffd9399e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-12669211-70db-53f2-9325-6e1ec5835553" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8a92539-674d-59a9-aa2a-68f113db4e17" "answer-12669211-70db-53f2-9325-6e1ec5835553" "answer-c527eec8-cb67-54f5-b73e-08cbe13ad25c" "answer-c7fa11db-9788-537c-8a72-0aede63cc2a7" "answer-6f38d0bc-036c-5a3d-8b34-69100927b81a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8a92539-674d-59a9-aa2a-68f113db4e17" :answer/id #uuid "e8a92539-674d-59a9-aa2a-68f113db4e17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1}+{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12669211-70db-53f2-9325-6e1ec5835553" :answer/id #uuid "12669211-70db-53f2-9325-6e1ec5835553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c527eec8-cb67-54f5-b73e-08cbe13ad25c" :answer/id #uuid "c527eec8-cb67-54f5-b73e-08cbe13ad25c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3}-{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7fa11db-9788-537c-8a72-0aede63cc2a7" :answer/id #uuid "c7fa11db-9788-537c-8a72-0aede63cc2a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{1}-{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f38d0bc-036c-5a3d-8b34-69100927b81a" :answer/id #uuid "6f38d0bc-036c-5a3d-8b34-69100927b81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3}-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-502fa5ed-8192-5239-85ce-b51fd4a6a69d" :question/id #uuid "502fa5ed-8192-5239-85ce-b51fd4a6a69d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89747" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21}, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(3<X<4).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<4) & =P(3<X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}-4}{21}-\\frac{{3}^{2}-4}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b0b3092-8249-5f35-a2f6-31dcce7858c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b0b3092-8249-5f35-a2f6-31dcce7858c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0b3092-8249-5f35-a2f6-31dcce7858c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a710d925-f2d3-59de-a577-1ad51b028b06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8798db5a-c6d4-56be-a275-6e7ec6c07b4f" "answer-a710d925-f2d3-59de-a577-1ad51b028b06" "answer-14cb2e76-8027-5b58-bb92-91643b6d3815" "answer-d4131973-c13d-5487-b2ad-0c1861102e99" "answer-a46bd425-c7b0-500c-a2c5-f64e18a9b985"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8798db5a-c6d4-56be-a275-6e7ec6c07b4f" :answer/id #uuid "8798db5a-c6d4-56be-a275-6e7ec6c07b4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a710d925-f2d3-59de-a577-1ad51b028b06" :answer/id #uuid "a710d925-f2d3-59de-a577-1ad51b028b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14cb2e76-8027-5b58-bb92-91643b6d3815" :answer/id #uuid "14cb2e76-8027-5b58-bb92-91643b6d3815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4131973-c13d-5487-b2ad-0c1861102e99" :answer/id #uuid "d4131973-c13d-5487-b2ad-0c1861102e99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a46bd425-c7b0-500c-a2c5-f64e18a9b985" :answer/id #uuid "a46bd425-c7b0-500c-a2c5-f64e18a9b985" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4" :question/id #uuid "de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126176" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<4 \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>6).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-(1-\\frac{16}{{6}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-270571a9-0f7f-511a-a143-fe6af5a15b80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-270571a9-0f7f-511a-a143-fe6af5a15b80" :answer-field/id #uuid "270571a9-0f7f-511a-a143-fe6af5a15b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ad797bab-2e14-55d8-85ab-5c933d18a216" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2e1f547c-1869-547c-823e-9966458b8f4a" "answer-ee6abc14-8e45-5ccc-b78f-b12ee121bb95" "answer-ad797bab-2e14-55d8-85ab-5c933d18a216" "answer-b0aaacdf-cb18-5d4c-8295-8a9b43dede71" "answer-8d811409-dae2-5c13-9164-8ada023a305c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e1f547c-1869-547c-823e-9966458b8f4a" :answer/id #uuid "2e1f547c-1869-547c-823e-9966458b8f4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee6abc14-8e45-5ccc-b78f-b12ee121bb95" :answer/id #uuid "ee6abc14-8e45-5ccc-b78f-b12ee121bb95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad797bab-2e14-55d8-85ab-5c933d18a216" :answer/id #uuid "ad797bab-2e14-55d8-85ab-5c933d18a216" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0aaacdf-cb18-5d4c-8295-8a9b43dede71" :answer/id #uuid "b0aaacdf-cb18-5d4c-8295-8a9b43dede71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d811409-dae2-5c13-9164-8ada023a305c" :answer/id #uuid "8d811409-dae2-5c13-9164-8ada023a305c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135186 :tutorial/content "The cumulative distribution function (or CDF) of a continuous random variable is defined the same way as for a discrete random variable. \n\nGiven a continuous random variable $X,$ the CDF is the function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nIf our random variable has the probability density function (or PDF) $f(x),$ then we have\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^x f(t) \\, \\textrm dt.\n$$\n\nNote that we use $f(t)dt$ in the integrand because $x$ serves as the upper limit of integration. \n\nFor example, consider the random variable $X$ with the following PDF:\n\n![](images/e7/e79c230f2b548c9280425f555f6d99a8f997e989289a05fb5f4584b656c4dcc8.svg)\n\nSince $f(x)= 0$ for all $x < 0,$  we have\n\n$$\nF(x)  = \\int_{-\\infty}^x 0 \\, \\textrm dt = 0\n$$\n\nif $x<0.$\n\nTo compute the CDF for $x\\geq 0,$  we integrate $f(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{2}{\\pi (1+{t}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing our CDF as a function defined over the entire real line, we get\n\n![](images/66/66b7bf54271075ae72fcf07fa4dc8573a94e97c2b2cc77680c0ec94b6053f360.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135187 :tutorial/content "When a random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive on the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b$ only, we have\n\n- $P(X \\leq x) = 0$ for $x < a,$ and\n\n- $P(X \\leq x) = 1$ for $x > b.$\n\nIn these cases, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/7a/7a64bac7c252a3f52fc92f6364edb5c66f31e47da28e78eeb0d069d894135700.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135188 :tutorial/content "As with discrete random variables, we can use the CDF of a continuous random variable to quickly compute a probability over an interval:\n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq b) = F(b) - F(a)\n$$\n\nFor example, suppose that a random variable $X$ has the following CDF:\n\n$$\nF(x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+e^{-x}}, \\qquad -\\infty < x < \\infty.\n$$\n\nWe can use the above CDF to quickly compute $P(0 \\leq x \\leq 1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le x\\le 1) & =F(1)-F(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-1}}-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-1}}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ≈0.231\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval, so we have\n\n$$\nP(0 \\leq X \\leq 1) = P(0 < X \\leq 1) = P(0 \\leq X < 1) = P(0 < X < 1) = 0.231.\n$$\n\nIn general, for a continuous random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq b) = P(a < X \\leq b) = P(a \\leq X < b) = P(a < X < b) = F(b) - F(a).\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134025 :activity/expected-seconds 1200.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
